# Vale quality-ratchet measurement config (created and removed by scripts/quality-ratchet.mjs)
/.vale-ratchet-measure-*.ini

# Worker PR-body scratch files (fleet-ops/0509#2609).
#
# One rule for the CLASS, not another exact spelling. This list has chased the
# same artifact four times — `pr-body.md`, `.pr-body.md`, `.fleet/pr-body-*.md`,
# `.pr-body-3095.md` — and `.fleet-pr-body.md` still reached main because it
# matched none of them. A glob per spelling loses to whoever names the next one
# differently.
/*pr-body*.md
/.*pr-body*.md
# Same scratch files when a lane writes them beside its plan. They are the PR
# body text, which already lives on GitHub, so committing one only adds a
# second copy for reviewers and for the `Vale` prose gate to disagree with
# (0509#3138: a committed `.fleet/pr-body-2985.md` failed `vale` on the word
# "granularity" after every code check had passed).
.fleet/pr-body-*.md

# 0509#3682: the whole .fleet/ directory is agent scratch — plans, phase
# handoffs, reviewer packets, burst scripts, salvage records, per-PR bodies.
# 55 of them had accumulated on main. None is read by app, workers, scripts,
# tests or any workflow; the one code reference (weekly-business-metrics.mjs)
# is a comment citing a burst script by name.
# NOT ignored, deliberately: .lane/reports/<branch>.md. Those are the lane
# evidence records, and tests/lane-evidence-collision.test.ts enforces the
# one-file-per-lane shape by listing them with `git ls-files --cached --others
# --exclude-standard`. Ignoring that path would empty the guard's input and
# make it pass on nothing.
.fleet/

# Per-PR body drafts at the repo root. /pr-body.md and /.pr-body.md were
# already covered; the numbered form was not, so .pr-body-3095.md and six
# siblings were committed to main.
/.pr-body-*.md

